[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1170","stub":{"id":"1170","section":"Route 9 & 123 to Hillsboro Fire Sta","altname":"","river":"Contoocook, N. Branch","difficulty":"V","states":["USA-NHM"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"6.98","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"517","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Rivers of the lower Contoocook region","distance":"0","photoID":"2131","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"This rapid was named after a lost camera part carried by Scott Underhill in one of the first descents back in the 80's. This rapid deserves a good scouting. Take out on river right about two ledge drops below the small concrete bridge and scout. The rapid takes a hard right through a shallow rocky drop then takes a left dropping precipitously over three ledge drops. The final drop contains a tight slot that is often clogged with wood. The most common run is boofing a rocky pourover to the left of the slot.","id":"1243","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Lost Lens","distance":"1.3","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":"5660"},{"type":"access","description":"When the roadway reappears on river left look for the Stone Bridge downstream. The river right arch is easier, taking the river left arch descent takes you through three rather sticky holes one after another. Get ready to punch your way through or work your way out of them. Most boaters chose to take out here at the bridge then shuttle around the 1.2 mile flat swampy section to the next rapid.","id":"1244","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Stone Bridge","distance":"1.7","photoID":"5664","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"There are two options here. This is amoung the toughest rapid in southern NH. The North Branch splits just after a long flat section leading down from Stone Bridge rapid. The right channel is shorter in distance but drops more dramatically over this distance. Scout from river right. The left channel is longer and narrower but still packs a punch. The initial drop is about 5' from a deteriorating rock dam, the river then takes a sharp right and drops steeply over the 1000+ feet in lenght. Along the way there are many pinning spots in this narrow channel. Always scout this drop since a fallen tree could easily block the entire channel.","id":"1245","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"The Mill Race","distance":"3","photoID":"0","difficulty":"V","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"This is a rather long complicated rapid. There are many channels and routes to chose from. Be especially cautious of wood here since some channels are very narrow and blind. Most of the rapid can be viewed from Liberty Farm Road which follows on river left most of the way.","id":"1246","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Liberty Farm","distance":"4.3","photoID":"5666","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"The Cleaver is the final drop on a rather long stretch of mostly class III and IV rapids. This one is difficult to scout from the river bank because of the steep bank and lack of eddies above. It is easily scouted from the takeout and route 9 which follows on river right. The best route to take over the Cleaver is about 8' from the river right bank. From here you will drop a few vertical feet. Do not run the center because the water piles up behind and under the enormous cleaver boulder. The run on river left is possible but is more difficult than the right side.","id":"1247","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"The Cleaver","distance":"5.8","photoID":"5665","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101253862","title":null,"post_date":"2018-10-09 04:00:00+00","detail":"New STRAINER: Millrace, L-side at top, first drop after entrance sluice. Large tree tilting into mid-channel from the island (between L-side and R-side Millrace). We were unable to move it without come-along, pry-bar, or chain-saw on Friday, October 5, 2018. The two posted pictures shows strainers near the camera which were removed, and the large remaining strainer fallen from across the channel.","user":{"name":"David Su"}},{"id":"100974230","title":null,"post_date":"2009-07-27 04:00:00+00","detail":"I was scouting the left side of Mill Race on July 25 and found three river wide strainers.","user":{"name":"Paul Reilly"}}],"photos":[{"id":"9193","ext":"b","post_id":"6148","description":"Top half of Corkscrew on the North Branch. Heniker gage at 8.8","caption":"North Branch: Contoocook","poi_name":"Corkscrew - loverns mill left","subject":"Nate Lesh-Hewey","author":"Moodus","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9193","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9193"}},{"id":"889962","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892442","description":"Left-side Millrace near the top","caption":"Strainer Oct 2018","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"David Su","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/889962","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/889962"}},{"id":"5662","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"Buried at Lost Lens","poi_name":"Lost Lens","subject":"Butch Mixon","author":"Mark Lacroix","poi_id":"1243","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5662","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5662"}},{"id":"889961","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892441","description":"in Millrace, L-side, fallen from the island.  The strainers in the water near the camera have been removed but not the big one.","caption":"Strainer, Oct.2018","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"David Su","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/889961","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/889961"}},{"id":"5663","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"North Branch Contoocook","poi_name":"Lost Lens","subject":"Butch Mixon","author":"Mark Lacroix","poi_id":"1243","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5663","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5663"}},{"id":"5666","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"Liberty Farm","poi_name":"Liberty Farm","subject":"Rand and Bill","author":"Sharon Lacroix","poi_id":"1246","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5666","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5666"}},{"id":"5661","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"Allan at Lost Lens","poi_name":"Lost Lens","subject":"Allan Bergren","author":"Mark Lacroix","poi_id":"1243","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5661","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5661"}},{"id":"5667","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"Rand at Lost Lens","poi_name":"Lost Lens","subject":"Rand Currier","author":"Mark Lacroix","poi_id":"1243","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5667","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5667"}},{"id":"5668","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"Stone Bridge","poi_name":"Stone Bridge","subject":"Jim","author":"","poi_id":"1244","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5668","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5668"}},{"id":"5660","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"Lost Lens NB of the Contoocook","poi_name":"Lost Lens","subject":"Allan Bergren","author":"Mark Lacrois","poi_id":"1243","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5660","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5660"}},{"id":"5664","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"Stone Bridge Rapid","poi_name":"Stone Bridge","subject":"Butch Mixon","author":"Mark Lacroix","poi_id":"1244","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5664","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5664"}},{"id":"5665","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3593","description":"","caption":"The Cleaver","poi_name":"The Cleaver","subject":"Mark Lacroix","author":"Sharon Lacroix","poi_id":"1245","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5665","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5665"}},{"id":"11010","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7801","description":"This picture was taken from about 50 yards down the rapid.  Level was about 9.4'. A word of warning: there is much more gradient in this rapid than the picutre suggests. A little bit more water can add substantial difficulty to Mill Race.  ","caption":"Left Channel Mill Race - Middle to Bottom at 9.4'","poi_name":"Mill Race","subject":"Left Channel Mill Race - Middle to Botton at 9.4","author":"Rob Stiles","poi_id":"517","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11010","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11010"}},{"id":"11009","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7801","description":"This photo was taken about 50 yards down from the entry of the left channel of Mill Race.  The entry drop is a narrow, steep four foot drop over the remains of an old dam. It's just out of site at the top left behind the abutments. A word of warning: there is a lot more gradient in this rapid than the picture suggests! The level is about 9.4'.  Just a little bit more water can make this rapid significantly more difficult!","caption":"Left Channel Mill Race - Top Portion at 9.4'","poi_name":"Mill Race","subject":"","author":"Rob Stiles","poi_id":"517","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11009","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11009"}},{"id":"13740","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8096","description":"Driving by on my way back from the warner saw some boaters coming down so I snapped some pics.","caption":"Nailing river right boof line on The Cleaver","poi_name":"The Cleaver","subject":"Daniel Abraham","author":"Nate Lesch-Huie","poi_id":"1247","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13740","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13740"}},{"id":"11018","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7801","description":"Pictured is the 15 or so yards of lead in just before you get to the slide.  (The photographer is standing right at the top of the slide.) ","caption":"Entry into the right channel of Mill Race","poi_name":"Mill Race, Right Channel","subject":"The lead in to the slide/falls in the righ channel of Mill Race","author":"Rob Stiles","poi_id":"517","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11018","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11018"}},{"id":"11017","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7801","description":"Pictured is the 20 or so yards of lead in just before you get to the slide.  (The photographer is standing at the lip of the slide.)","caption":"Entry into the right channel of Mill Race - oversized pic","poi_name":"Mill Race, Right Channel","subject":"The lead in to the slide/falls in the righ channel of Mill Race","author":"Rob Stiles","poi_id":"517","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11017","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11017"}},{"id":"11016","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7801","description":"Pictured is \"Danger\" Dave Amato running the main drop of the right channel of Mill Race.  Though the right drop is definitely more dramatic, it's more straight forward than the left.  Just don't mess up the lead in.  Beware of debris that often accumulates in the pool at the base of this slide. ","caption":"Right Channel - Mill Race - main drop - at 9.4'","poi_name":"Mill Race, Right Channel","subject":"An Unknown Stylin' Mill Race Rapid","author":"Rob Stiles","poi_id":"517","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11016","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11016"}}],"detail":{"id":"1170","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Information from Greg and Sue Hanlon's [Steep Creeks of New England](http://www.npmb.com/bookshop/bookshop.htm), additions by Nate Warren\n\nFrom Concord, NH, take I-89 North to Exit 5. Follow Rte. 9-202 to Hillsborough. Continue through Hillsborough, Lower Village to North Branch Village, where Rte. 9 crosses the North Branch.  To the putin from North Branch Village follow Rte. 9 ~5 miles to a small pull-off just after a set of powerlines across Rte. 9, as you are driving up a hill.  Park by a gated, overgrown farm road on the left. Carry past the gate, down the farm road, and through the overgrown path.  Veer left at the first fork in the path, and look close for the path on the right after another 100 yards.\n\nTo takeout: follow Rte. 9 back toward North Branch Village (in Antrim). Take out at the junction of Rte. 31 (where 31 breaks off of 9 and heads south) and Rte. 9, below The Cleaver.\n\n[Click here for a GoogleMap of the run, including access points (and scouting points)](https://www.google.com/maps/dir/North+Branch+Village+Antiques+%26+Accessories/43.0803857,-71.9957663/43.073991,-72.0191123/43.0743369,-72.0454331/43.0663482,-72.0570023/@43.0689191,-72.0287211,4978m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m12!4m11!1m5!1m1!1s0x0:0x7c88c91be7c57236!2m2!1d-71.981541!2d43.075093!1m0!1m0!1m0!1m0!3e0)\n\n**Warning:** this run may contain thick ice in the early Spring; it tends to break up later than many other, steeper runs.\n\nThe NB Took is a class IV (2@V) creek in southern NH.  It has a large, swampy drainage, which means it holds water far better than most other creeks in NH.  The upper section has long zig-zagging class four rapids with big pools at the bottom.  The largest rapid, Lost Lens, is class V- at good levels.  Soon after Lost Lens is \"Stone Bridge,\" a class III where the river passes under an old stone bridge, then under Route 9.  Below here is a mile or so of class II-III, which is really fun if the level is not low, followed by flatwater and then Mill Race.\n\nMill Race is the highlight of the North Branch.  The left is a 100+ yard class V rapid that ends with a difficult crux move.  This one collects lost of wood.  The right side is a steep 20' slide with a scrapey entrance.  The slide is class V-.\n\nBelow Mill Race the river drops under Loveren Mill Road (a good place to scout, while you are dry, or for park & huck...), then into over a mile of flatwater, including a marshy swamp.  If you are running the NB at lower levels, the swamp can become difficult to navigate.  Some people drive shuttle around it, taking off at Loveren Mill Rd. and putting back on at Liberty Farm Road.\n\nLiberty Farm rapid is the first rapid after the flatwater.  It is a long class IV with many lines.  After a mile or so of class II-III, the river returns to the road for the last rapid, \"Cleaver.\"  From the top the water exploding up in the center-left of the river is the spot to avoid.  There is a far-left line, but generally boaters try to stay right of the Cleaver and far enough off the right side to avoid the submerged ledge at the bottom.  Takeout below Cleaver, climb up the embankment & careful crossing the road!","averageGradient":"55","maxGradient":null,"length":"8","correlations":[{"reachID":"1170","isPrimary":false,"correlationDetails":null,"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"gaugeInfo":{"name":"NORTH BRANCH RIVER NEAR ANTRIM, NH","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01084000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ARCHIVED","latestFlowReading":{"value":"61.3","dateTime":"2011-07-06T03:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.36","dateTime":"2011-07-06T03:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"43.0817464","longitude":"-71.9784147"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01084000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01084000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"comment":"This is a new gage that just went on line in September of 09.  Corrolations are still to be determined.  ","status":{"status":"stale","latestReading":{"value":"61.3","dateTime":"2011-07-06T03:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}},{"reachID":"1170","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"8.5","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"12"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"CONTOOCOOK RIVER NEAR HENNIKER, NH","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01085000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"813","dateTime":"2026-05-12